  "aiContextParagraph": "A major storm system across the United States has severely disrupted Thanksgiving holiday activities. In New York City, the annual Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade was postponed due to safety concerns regarding the weather. The system brought torrential rain, high winds, and flooding to the East Coast, while heavy snow impacted the Midwest. According to reports, more than 900,000 utility customers experienced power outages, with the highest concentrations reported in Pennsylvania and Virginia. Travel has also been significantly affected, with nearly 400 flights canceled and over 2,000 delayed, predominantly at East Coast airports. Emergency teams have been deployed to assist residents in coastal regions affected by floodwaters. The weather event also coincided with a scheduled slate of NFL games, including matchups featuring the Bears, Lions, Eagles, Cowboys, Chiefs, and Bills.",
